speechtext:
In connection with the item for replacing buildings and equipment destroyed by fire at Esquimalt, I would point out that a number of workmen who were employed at the place at that particular time had their tools stored there, and they were all destroyed in the fire, entailing a very severe loss in many cases. These men are not rich;
Supply-Public Works

they are men working for wages, and I would like to know if the government does not intend to make any provision for compensating them in full or in part for the loss of the tools destroyed at that time.
